Your project uses **MSTest v2 (2.2.10)**. Here's what needs to change for v3:

---

### 1. Update packages (`TestProject.csproj`)
Replace the three individual packages with the unified `MSTest` metapackage:

```xml
<!-- Remove these three -->
<PackageReference Include="MSTest.TestFramework" Version="2.2.10" />
<PackageReference Include="MSTest.TestAdapter" Version="2.2.10" />
<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.5.0" />

<!-- Add this one -->
<PackageReference Include="MSTest" Version="3.8.0" />
```

### 2. Fix assertion overloads (`UserServiceTests.cs`)
v3 removed `Assert.AreEqual(object, object)` and `Assert.AreSame(object, object)`. Add generic type parameters:

```csharp
// Line 13 — before:
Assert.AreEqual(expected, actual);
// After:
Assert.AreEqual<object>(expected, actual);

// Line 20 — before:
Assert.AreSame(obj, obj);
// After:
Assert.AreSame<object>(obj, obj);
```

### 3. Fix `DataRow` type mismatch (`UserServiceTests.cs`)
v3 enforces strict type matching. Lines 24–25 pass `long` literals (`1L`, `2L`) but the parameter is `int`:

```csharp
// Before:
[DataRow(1L, "Alice")]
[DataRow(2L, "Bob")]
public void GetUserName_ReturnsCorrectName(int id, string expectedName)

// Fix — either change literals to int:
[DataRow(1, "Alice")]
[DataRow(2, "Bob")]

// Or change the parameter to long:
public void GetUserName_ReturnsCorrectName(long id, string expectedName)
```

### 4. Timeout behavior change
`[Timeout(3000)]` on line 32 is still valid, but v3 unifies timeout behavior across .NET Core and Framework. Verify the 3-second timeout still suits your test after upgrading.

---

### No TFM change needed
`net6.0` is supported by MSTest v3, so no target framework update is required (though consider `net8.0` for LTS support since .NET 6 is end-of-life).

